* Short full-modulator transient bench (issue #125) -- circuit body for `klt sim`
* (no .lib/.control/.end: klt sim owns those; corner = process/temp/Vdda).
* Generated from this template by make_request.py -- edit the template, not the deck.
*
* Circuit under test: design/modulator/modulator.spice (clkgen + 2x integrator
* + comparator + SR latch) with design/ota/ota_fd.spice and
* design/modulator/comparator/comparator.spice, exactly the include list
* design/modulator/README.md "Consuming the netlists" prescribes. The
* standalone integrator/clkgen netlists are deliberately NOT included: the
* top-level netlist already defines both subcircuits.
*
* Boundary (DR-005, all ideal): VCM 0.9 V, VREFP/VREFN 1.5/0.3 V (VREF =
* 1.2 V differential), ibias 5 uA. VCM is held at 0.9 V on every corner, as
* the other transistor-level benches in this repo do; it does not track Vdda.
*
* Stimulus: a single coherent tone, @AMP@ V peak per side about VCM, so the
* differential input peak is twice that, which is @DBFS@ dBFS against the
* 1.2 V differential reference (model B's full scale; spec row 11 and sec 5.4
* both put the peak differential input at 0.5*VREF = 0.6 V). Tone frequency
* @FIN@ Hz is @CYCLES@ whole cycles over the @NREC@ recorded modulator
* clocks, so the record is coherent. The sine runs from t = 0 with zero
* phase, so u(t) = 2*@AMP@*sin(2*pi*@FIN@*t) volts differential exactly --
* the input sequence is reproducible without any waveform file.
*
* Clock: @FS@ Hz, 50 % duty, 0.2 ns edges, first rising 50 % crossing at
* @TRISE0@ s. `Vclk` is declared as a corners.supply_v key and listed in
* corners.supply_waveforms, so klt rescales its PULSE levels per corner and
* the clock swings to that corner's Vdda instead of a fixed 1.8 V. A clock
* that did not track the supply would leave the clkgen input inverter
* partially on at Vdda = 1.98 V and pollute the row 13 power number.
.options gmin=1e-9
.include "../../design/ota/ota_fd.spice"
.include "../../design/modulator/comparator/comparator.spice"
.include "../../design/modulator/modulator.spice"
Vdda vdda 0 1.8
Vvcm vcm 0 0.9
Vrefp vrefp 0 1.5
Vrefn vrefn 0 0.3
Ibias vdda ibias 5u
Vclk clk 0 PULSE(0 1.8 @TCLK0@ 0.2n 0.2n @PW@ @TPER@)
Vinp vinp 0 SIN(0.9 @AMP@ @FIN@ 0 0 0)
Vinn vinn 0 SIN(0.9 @AMP@ @FIN@ 0 0 180)
Xmod vdda 0 vinp vinn vrefp vrefn vcm ibias clk bs modulator
* Differential integrator outputs, as model B's x1 and x2 appear in volts.
Bo1d o1d 0 V='v(xmod.o1p)-v(xmod.o1n)'
Bo2d o2d 0 V='v(xmod.o2p)-v(xmod.o2n)'
* Instantaneous power delivered by each ideal boundary source, in watts
* carried on a voltage node (SPICE has no power node). SPICE reports a
* source's current as positive into its positive terminal, so the power the
* source delivers is -v*i.
Bpvdda pvdda 0 V='-v(vdda)*i(vdda)'
Bpref  pref  0 V='-(v(vrefp)*i(vrefp)+v(vrefn)*i(vrefn))'
Bpvcm  pvcm  0 V='-v(vcm)*i(vvcm)'
* P_ana as spec row 13 is graded here: the VDDA rail (which already carries
* the 5 uA bias current, since Ibias is fed from vdda) plus the reference
* current. The vcm source is reported separately and is NOT in this sum.
Bpana  pana  0 V='v(pvdda)+v(pref)'
